  "body": "Sorry in advance if its in wrong place\r\n\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello, thanks in advance, I joined the big cybersecurity channel with my homeserver, then I left directly because I didn't want to federate with this specific homeserver. so I whitelisted only the servers I wanted to federate but how long do the other servers from the cybersecurity room make requests to try to federate even if i have left the room ? \r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- join a very big room\r\n- direct leave \r\n- whitelist only the servers you want to federate\r\n- watch all the servers try to federate \r\n\r\n<!--\r\nDescribe how what happens differs from what you expected.\r\n\r\nI wish the servers would stop federating me when i have left the room. \r\n\r\ni have this type (*) of requests all the time now and before i only have the users of my homeservers making requests.\r\n\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\nlatest docker version.\r\n\r\n(*) example : \r\n\r\nsynapse.federation.transport.server._base - 277 - WARNING - PUT-9733 - authenticate_request failed: 403: Federation denied with cadair.com.\r\n\r\nsynapse.http.server - 95 - INFO - PUT-9733 - <XForwardedForRequest at 0x7fecebbbb550 method='PUT' uri='/matrix_/federation/v1/send/1643016771382' clientproto='HTTP/1.0' site='8008'> SynapseError: 403 - Federation denied with cadair.com\r\n\r\n",
